","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BigRoy/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BigRoy/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BigRoy/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BigRoy","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ynput/ayon-frontend/commits/f914778a8badc72c224e727eacec6b95b06faff5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T21:08:05Z","email":"roy_nieterau@hotmail.com","name":"Roy Nieterau"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T21:08:05Z","email":"roy_nieterau@hotmail.com","name":"Roy Nieterau"},"message":"feat(tables): sort by multiple keys\n\nThe backend accepts a list of sortBy keys (ynput/ayon-backend#1141), so the\noverview, lists, versions/products and projects tables can now be sorted by\nup to five columns.\n\n- Sort is its own page in the Customize panel: reorder, flip and remove the\n  sort keys, and add further ones.\n- Shift+click on a column''s sort button adds it as a further key, and sorted\n  headers show their position when there is more than one key.\n- Views store sortBy as a list where ''-'' marks a descending key. Views saved\n  with a single sortBy and sortDesc still load.\n- The paginated queries declare sortBy as [String!], which needs a backend\n  with multi-key sorting.","tree":{"sha":"bb2ac5f7b690830809985d1b18f936b0d55d8922","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ynput/ayon-frontend/git/trees/bb2ac5f7b690830809985d1b18f936b0d55d8922"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ynput/ayon-frontend/git/commits/f914778a8badc72c224e727eacec6b95b06faff5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2439881?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BigRoy/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BigRoy/followers","following_url":"https://api.gi