.com/users/Innders/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Innders/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Innders/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Innders/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Innders","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ynput/ayon-frontend/commits/d8b2c86e4d0fd4855b51c5d833a8786d371dad9f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T11:57:33Z","email":"49156310+Innders@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Innders"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T11:57:33Z","email":"49156310+Innders@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Innders"},"message":"fix(shared): only focus the comment editor when the user opens it\n\nThe editor''s autoFocus was derived from the attached annotations and\nfiles, so it could flip to true while the input was already open (e.g.\nwhen the annotation list changed) and steal focus mid-session. Keys\nmeant for the player, like the O out-point shortcut, then got typed\ninto the comment. It also opened focused for restored drafts.\n\nNow the editor only takes focus when the user clicks to open it, duplicates\na comment, or edits one. Opening because of a new annotation or a restored\ndraft leaves focus where it was.","tree":{"sha":"42648af52ee98ac0e00a8a479c4bc714f42b843a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ynput/ayon-frontend/git/trees/42648af52ee98ac0e00a8a479c4bc714f42b843a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ynput/ayon-frontend/git/commits/d8b2c86e4d0fd4855b51c5d833a8786d371dad9f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/49156310?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Innders/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Innders/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Innders/following{/oth