red{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/bitmakerla/estela/commit/b540a8e3e12707d3ab2bdf95598f6c61deb458e7","node_id":"C_kwDOG79c49oAKGI1NDBhOGUzZTEyNzA3ZDNhYjJiZGY5NTU5OGY2YzYxZGViNDU4ZTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/bitmakerla/estela/commit/2ccb67286a8dd3c1ef2ef7aaadbbd9e84719db71","sha":"2ccb67286a8dd3c1ef2ef7aaadbbd9e84719db71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bitmakerla/estela/commits/2ccb67286a8dd3c1ef2ef7aaadbbd9e84719db71"}],"sha":"b540a8e3e12707d3ab2bdf95598f6c61deb458e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bitmakerla/estela/commits/b540a8e3e12707d3ab2bdf95598f6c61deb458e7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10171343?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jc99k/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jc99k/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jc99k/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jc99k/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/jc99k","id":10171343,"login":"jc99k","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMTcxMzQz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jc99k/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jc99k/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jc99k/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jc99k/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jc99k/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jc99k","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bitmakerla/estela/commits/2ccb67286a8dd3c1ef2ef7aaadbbd9e84719db71/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T18:31:06Z","email":"10171343+jc99k@users.noreply.github.com","name":"JC Duenas"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T18:31:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"✨ feat: create MeteredUsageRecord model and functionality, including … (#283)\n\n* ✨ feat: create MeteredUsageRecord model and functionality, including Celery Beat and task to fetch from Redis\n\n* 🐛 fix: set `delta_proxy_bytes` as NULL only when proxy attribution does not apply, and 0 when proxy is configured and delta is zero\n\nAligned writes with the field help text: NULL only when proxy\nattribution does not apply (no proxy_name on the job and a zero delta);\n0 when a proxy is configured and the slice/close/reconcile delta is\nzero.\n\nImplementation: a shared helper\ndelta_proxy_bytes_for_flow_row(proxy_name_label, delta) in ledger.py\nused from both ledger.py (JOB_CLOSE / ADJUSTMENT) and hourly.py\n(DELTA_SLICE). We still persist non-zero proxy deltas when there is no\nconfigured proxy name so we do not drop Redis-reported bytes on\nmis-labeled jobs (Redis can show proxy traffic while the job record has\nno proxy name (legacy crawl, misconfiguration. Keeping non-zero values\npreserves bytes that Redis already counted, even when the job wasn’t\nlabeled with a provider name).\n\n* ⚡️ perf(metering): read Scrapy counters once per job close\n\nappend_metered_usage_for_job_close now calls read_scrapy_counters_from_redis once at the top, uses raw = … or {}, then derives storage_final and proxy_cumulative from that dict for both the non-hourly JOB_CLOSE path and the hourly reconcile path (so no duplicate hgetall). Removed the two per-field helpers. Kept the in-function from api.utils import read_scrapy_counters_from_redis so existing tests that patch api.utils.read_scrapy_counters_from_redis still apply. Ledger tests still pass.\n\n* 📝 docs(models): clarify signed delta_storage_bytes for billing consumers\n\ndocument on MeteredUsageRecord.delta_storage_bytes that storage flow is a signed Redis cumulative diff: object byte totals can shrink, so negatives are expected; warns downstream billing/analytics not to filter or aggregate as if values were always positive (e.g. strict > 0 filters drop legitimate corrections). No runtime or schema change.\n\n* ⚡️ perf(metering): avoid refresh_from_db in metered_proxy_name_from_job\n\nmetered_proxy_name_from_job no longer runs refresh_from_db on every call (removes an extra SELECT proxy_usage_data per hourly slice and other hot paths). It only uses the job instance in memory; the docstring says to refresh first if DB consistency matters. append_metered_usage_for_job_close still does a single refresh_from_db(fields=[\"proxy_usage_data\"]) before resolving the proxy label so close/reconcile rows stay defensive without N queries per tick.\n\n* 🐛 fix(test): add config.settings.test and pytest pythonpath\n\nAdd config/settings/test.py so DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE = config.settings.test (already in pytest.ini) resolves in git: SQLite in-memory DB, in-process Celery, estela_queue_adapter stubbed before importing base, and literal spiderdata settings so dummy env values do not break imports. Adds config/settings/__init__.py so config.settings is a proper package. Updates pytest.ini with pythonpath = .. so database_adapters at the repo root is on the path when pytest runs from estela-api/, matching how local/CI runs are documented. No change to deployed Django settings (local / Helm).\n\n* ✨ feat(metering): make MeteredUsageRecords generalized to use any payload\n\n* 📝 docs: add Metering Usage Records POST API endpoint documentation\n\n* 🐛 fix: Validate metering project IDs before permission queries, reuse the serializer-resolved project during ingest, narrow Redis cleanup exception handling, align hourly Celery schedules, and collapse unreleased metering migrations","tree":{"sha":"e9b94802523154b12b02a3279acb4561a564cdde","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bitmakerla/estela/git/trees/e9b94802523154b12b02a3279acb4561a564cdde"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/bitmakerla/estela/git/commits/2ccb67286a8dd3c1ef2ef7aaadbbd9e84719db71","verification":{"payload":"tree e9b94802523154b12b02a3279acb4561a564cdde\nparent 796452c5a4f19a31e4a465bfea3e4d62ccd6ff37\nauthor JC Duenas <10171343+jc99k@users.noreply.github.com> 1784140266 -0500\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1784140266 -0500\n\n✨ feat: create MeteredUsageRecord model and functionality, including … (#283)\n\n* ✨ feat: create MeteredUsageRecord model and functionality, including Celery Beat and task to fetch from Redis\n\n* 🐛 fix: set `delta_proxy_bytes` as NULL only when proxy attribution does not apply, and 0 when proxy is configured and delta is zero\n\nAligned writes with the field help text: NULL only when proxy\nattribution does not apply (no proxy_name on the job and a zero delta);\n0 when a proxy is configured and the slice/close/reconcile delta is\nzero.\n\nImplementation: a shared helper\ndelta_proxy_bytes_for_flow_row(proxy_name_label, delta) in ledger.py\nused from both ledger.py (JOB_CLOSE / ADJUSTMENT) and hourly.py\n(DELTA_SLICE). We still persist non-zero proxy deltas when there is no\nconfigured proxy name so we do not drop Redis-reported bytes on\nmis-labeled jobs (Redis can show proxy traffic while the job record has\nno proxy name (legacy crawl, misconfiguration. Keeping non-zero values\npreserves bytes that Redis already counted, even when the job wasn’t\nlabeled with a provider name).\n\n* ⚡️ perf(metering): read Scrapy counters once per job close\n\nappend_metered_usage_for_job_close now calls read_scrapy_counters_from_redis once at the top, uses raw = … or {}, then derives storage_final and proxy_cumulative from that dict for both the non-hourly JOB_CLOSE path and the hourly reconcile path (so no duplicate hgetall). Removed the two per-field helpers. Kept the in-function from api.utils import read_scrapy_counters_from_redis so existing tests that patch api.utils.read_scrapy_counters_from_redis still apply. Ledger tests still pass.\n\n* 📝 docs(models): clarify signed delta_storage_bytes for billing consumers\n\ndocument on MeteredUsageRecord.delta_storage_bytes that storage flow is a signed Redis cumulative diff: object byte totals can shrink, so negatives are expected; warns downstream billing/analytics not to filter or aggregate as if values were always positive (e.g. strict > 0 filters drop legitimate corrections). No runtime or schema change.\n\n* ⚡️ perf(metering): avoid refresh_from_db in metered_proxy_name_from_job\n\nmetered_proxy_name_from_job no longer runs refresh_from_db on every call (removes an extra SELECT proxy_usage_data per hourly slice and other hot paths). It only uses the job instance in memory; the docstring says to refresh first if DB consistency matters. append_metered_usage_for_job_close still does a single refresh_from_db(fields=[\"proxy_usage_data\"]) before resolving the proxy label so close/reconcile rows stay defensive without N queries per tick.\n\n* 🐛 fix(test): add config.settings.test and pytest pythonpath\n\nAdd config/settings/test.py so DJANGO_SETTINGS_MODULE = config.settings.test (already in pytest.ini) resolves in git: SQLite in-memory DB, in-process Celery, estela_queue_adapter stubbed before importing base, and literal spiderdata settings so dummy env values do not break imports. Adds config/settings/__init__.py so config.settings is a proper package. Updates pytest.ini with pythonpath = .. so database_adapters at the repo root is on the path when pytest runs from estela-api/, matching how local/CI runs are documented. No change to deployed Django settings (local / Helm).\n\n* ✨ feat(metering): make MeteredUsageRecords generalized to use any payload\n\n* 📝 docs: add Metering Usage Records POST API endpoint documentation\n\n* 🐛 fix: Validate metering project IDs before permission queries, reuse the serializer-resolved project during ingest, narrow Redis cleanup exception handling, align hourly Celery schedules, and collapse unreleased metering migrations","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqV9HqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAPBQ